', sources=['30+']. The 'source_spans' in the row_map entry should be the spans of the source bins. The 'source_spans' in the row_map entry is a list of [lo, hi] for each source in the 'sources' list. So for '5-11', sources=['<25'], source_spans=[[null, 24]]. For '25-29', sources=['25-29'], source_spans=[[25, 29]]. For '30', sources=['30+'], source_spans=[[30, null]]. The same logic applies to col_map. The source age bins are [40,49], [50,54], [55,59], [60,64], [65,null]. The target ages are single years. For target '50', it falls in [50,54], so sources=['50-54'], source_spans=[[50,54]]. For target '65', it falls in [65,null], so sources=['65 +'], source_spans=[[65, null]]. The 'transpose' is true because the source is Age x Service and target is Service x Age. The 'values_unit' is 'percent' because the source prints percentages. The 'derive' is null because no calculation is needed beyond the mapping and unit conversion. The 'notes' explain the mapping strategy."
}

